why Your Fire Totem for every fire totem, Searing Totem with it, and Forever's Totem of Charged Flames.

# Forever's Alliance (Dwarf) Call of Fire: Ingrid Dunwald in Kharanos or
# Eldrun Stormbreaker in Ironforge (94449) -> Bruegs Kindleborn in his cave
# above South Gate Outpost (94465: the Torch of the Dormant Flame) -> Braldir
# Ashmantle on the peak south of Thelsamar in Loch Modan (94466: Fire Tar from
# the Tunnel Rat Geomancers, a Reagent Pouch from the Stonesplinter Seers) ->
# the Fire Sapta and the Minor Manifestation of Fire on the Shrine of Eternal
# Flame (94467, the Brazier of the Dormant Flame) -> the lit Torch of Eternal
# Flame back to Bruegs (94468: the Fire Totem and the Totem of Charged Flames).
# Sources: quests.json, npcs.json, objects.json and items.json (givers,
# enders, droppers, the brazier); Forever's quest notes for the trails, the
# casters' spells, the respawns and the manifestation (level 12, immune to
# fire, single spawn, 3 min respawn, Glowing Ember every kill). The Fire Tar
# and Reagent Pouch have no drop rate for these two droppers in the data.
# Fire Sapta 94473 (Braldir) replaces a lost sapta.
# The leveling guide forever/alliance/dwarf-gnome/01-dun-morogh carries the
# chain inline; this guide does it in one go.

step Call of Fire
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip At 10 Ingrid Dunwald, the shaman trainer in Kharanos, or Eldrun Stormbreaker, the shaman trainer in Ironforge, sends you to Bruegs Kindleborn.
  level 10
  accept 94449                                -- Ingrid Dunwald, Kharanos; or Eldrun Stormbreaker, Ironforge

step Bruegs Kindleborn
  tip Follow the road east to the tunnel towards South Gate Outpost. Out of the first tunnel, keep left past Mountaineer Barleybrew and the tower: a slim trail, hard to see but shown on the minimap, winds up the mountain to Bruegs' cave above the farm. He hands you the Torch of the Dormant Flame: keep it until the end of the chain.
  turnin 94449                                -- Bruegs Kindleborn
  accept 94465

step Braldir Ashmantle
  zone Loch Modan
  tip From Bruegs' ledge you can drop carefully down the mountain into Loch Modan, or walk back through the tunnel. Braldir Ashmantle keeps the shrine on the peak just south of Thelsamar: a hidden trail along a cliff ledge, marked by stone totems, climbs to it from the road north of the peak.
  turnin 94465                                -- Braldir Ashmantle
  accept 94466

step Reagent Pouch
  tip The Stonesplinter Seers (level 13-14) stand among the troggs of Stonesplinter Valley in the south of the loch, and in the trogg camps north-east of Thelsamar. They throw Lightning Bolts from 40 yards and run for help when hurt: pull one at a time. Respawn about five minutes.
  collect 6652 quest 94466.2                  -- Reagent Pouch

step Fire Tar
  tip The Tunnel Rat Geomancers (level 12-13) work only inside the Silver Stream Mine at the north end of the loch, past Thelsamar. They cast Fire Blast behind a Fire Shield and run for help at low health.
  collect 5026 quest 94466.1                  -- Fire Tar

step Braldir Ashmantle
  tip Back up the trail to Braldir. He makes the Fire Sapta from the tar and the pouch: keep it with the torch.
  turnin 94466                                -- Braldir Ashmantle
  accept 94467

step Lost the Fire Sapta?
  when onquest 94467
  when !has 6636
  tip Only if the Fire Sapta is gone from your bags: Braldir gives you another.
  turnin 94473 direct                         -- Braldir Ashmantle: a new Fire Sapta

step The Shrine of Eternal Flame
  tip Climb on past Braldir to the peak. Drink the Fire Sapta beside the rock statue there to see the Minor Manifestation of Fire (level 12): it waits until you strike, but grows stronger the longer it is left, and it is immune to fire. Open at once with Rockbiter Weapon and Earth Shock. Its Glowing Ember drops every time.
  use 6636 quest 94467.1 @31.9,64.5           -- Fire Sapta, beside the statue
  collect 6655 quest 94467.1                  -- Glowing Ember: Minor Manifestation of Fire

step The Brazier of the Dormant Flame
  tip Click the Brazier of the Dormant Flame atop the shrine with the torch in your bags to place the ember, then click it again for the next quest: the lit Torch of Eternal Flame.
  turnin 94467                                -- Brazier of the Dormant Flame
  accept 94468

step Bruegs Kindleborn
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip Back through the South Gate tunnel and up the trail to Bruegs' cave. Keep the Fire Totem in your bags for good: every fire totem needs it.
  turnin 94468 reward 5176 263412             -- Bruegs Kindleborn: Searing Totem, your Fire Totem and the Totem of Charged Flames
  train class
